 there are critics who say the  opposite many commenters on my channel  are keen to dismiss Bruce as just an  actor several have stated that Bruce Lee  wouldn't stand a chance against the  modern MMA fighter I've no doubt he  would have been world champion in MMA no  there he's fluid he's loose he's fast  his movement is fluid it's efficient  it's functional so many guys are  addicted to strengthen conditioner he's  get balled up and stiff and slow and  Bruce was free his buddy was nimble  whether the latter statement is true is  up for debate of course there is  absolutely no denying Bruce Lee's talent  or power if you know anything about  martial arts then you only have to  witness one of his kicks dinner he was  supremely skilled and incredibly fast  and powerful footage of Bruce Lee's  sparring with a student has also  recently emerged online wonderfully  restored over at beardies YouTube  channel and while it isn't a flawless  performance it definitely demonstrates  the principles Bruce preached in highly  effective action in an unstated arena  likewise there's no denying that his  physique was one of the most striking of  the time another testament to his will  and dedication there are many rumors  regarding through his strength  Danny and Santo Jai Lewis and Jesse  Glover described Bruce as being able to  hold barbells of 72 125 pounds right out  in front of him with straight arms has  been said that he could puncture a can  of soda with a single finger and those  who experiences one-inch punch say that  it left him winded and injured is any of  this true  I find it suspect that there's no video  evidence of any of these skills  Bruce certainly wasn't shy of filming  himself or of self promoting if he could  jab a finger through a cola can wouldn't  we have seen it and lifting that much  weight with straight arms is incredibly  difficult but then again most of these  feats are possible and have been  accomplished by others the stories are  corroborated by more than one witness  and we know from his training with  overcoming isometrics that he could  generate a lot of power for his small  size and we know from this to finger  push-up that he had a very powerful  fingers so who knows  it's interesting to note though that the  one-inch punch was not really delivered  from an inch but rather from the length  of Bruce's outstretched fingers more  like four to five inches we can't know  for certain how Bruce Lee would perform  against modern fighters because we'll  never have the opportunity to set up  such a match the fact that he inspired  the fighting method with so many of them  used they should count for something  and it certainly disingenuous to  describe him as anything other than a  visionary skilled fighter none of this  is really the point though the point is  that Bruce Lee was magnetic enough and  obviously talented enough that he was  able to smash through prejudices open  closed minds and changed the status quo  were it not for Bruce Lee he likely  wouldn't have Jackie Chan the Karate Kid  martial arts classes all around the  world the matrix or such exposure to  Chinese philosophy it's no surprise that  he was named by Time magazine as one of  the hundred most influential people of  the 20th century and it's only fitting  that we pay homage to him here on the  bio near where our goals and interests  share much in common with the dragon  totally family's really useful  interesting guys if you did then please  leave a like and share it around that  helps me out immensely let me know in  the comments down below what you think  about Bruce Lee what inspires you about  his life story and also who'd likely to  cover in future like I say you can head  over to the patreon page if you want to  vote on who's gonna be covered in the  very next learning from legends episode  and in the meantime I have my video on  body language coming up very soon  followed shortly by my video on  Nightwing training and lots of other  cool stuff so if that all sounds cool  then thanks a ton for watching please  subscribe and I'll see you next time bye  for now
 

